    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d958">

                <pb facs="1208" n="1190" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.24/3–1346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-13T18:00:00-05:00">March 13, 1946—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Dept has notified Paraguayan representative of availability for their
                    purchase from surplus of military ground equipment for 1 Battalion of
                    Infantry.</p>
                <pb facs="1209" n="1191" xml:id="pg1191"/>
                <p>Details concerning prices and terms to be arranged by Paraguayan representatives
                    directly with Foreign Liquidation Commission.</p>
                <p>Above equipment excludes some civilian items, particularly motor vehicles, not
                    now available in surplus.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
